    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0390" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg310"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Hart</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 421.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram of
                    August 27, and previous instructions, regarding the expropriation of the
                    property of American citizens by the military authorities of Colombia, and the
                    bearing thereon of the stipulations of Article VIII of the treaty of 1846, I
                    inclose copy of a dispatch from the United States vice-consul-general at Panama
                    reporting instances occuring near Cali.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>





